hadiths[43]{hadithnumber,text}:
"483","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) to Yemen. Then he narrated the entire hadith, in which there is: \Allah Almighty has made Zakat obligatory on their wealth"," which should be collected from their rich and distributed among their needy and poor.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim) The words are Bukhari's."""
"484","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (RA) that Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) wrote this text to Hazrat Anas (RA) regarding the duty of Zakat which the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had prescribed for the Muslims and which Allah (SWT) ordered to His Messenger: \There are goats for twenty-four camels or less\"""," one goat for every five camels. When the number reaches twenty-five to thirty-five"," bint mukhaz (one-year-old) camels will be required for this number. If he is not available"," then Ibn Lubun (two years old) male child will be obligatory. And when the number reaches from thirty-six to forty-five"," then a Bint Lubun (two-year-old) camel will be placed among them. When the number reaches from forty-six to sixty"," among them"," a young she-camel of three years old"," capable of mating"," will be responsible. When they reach from sixty-one to seventy-five"," Jizaa (four-year-old camel) will be required among them. When the number is from seventy-six to ninety"," two bint-lubun (two two-year-old two-year-old camels) will be born among them. When the number reaches from ninety-one to one hundred and twenty"," two rights (three three-year-old two young camels) must be paid in them"," which are equal to a pair of camels. And when the number becomes more than one hundred and twenty"," then Bint Lubun (two-year-old camels) and Haqqa (three-year-old camels) will be wajib on every forty camels. And whoever has only four camels"," then there is no zakat on that number unless their owner wishes. Zakat of goats \""that graze outside (in the forest and desert)\"" from forty to one hundred and twenty goats"," only one goat will be collected in Zakat. When this number increases from one hundred and twenty to two hundred"," two goats will be received in Zakat. Then when it reaches three hundred from two hundred"," three goats will be received. When the number exceeds three hundred"," one goat will be collected as Zakat for every hundred. If one has less than forty goats grazing in the forest outside"," then there is no Zakat on the owner unless the owner so desires. And different animals should not be brought together for fear of Zakat"," and animals together should not be separated. And the animals that are shared by two people"," then they should calculate jointly (after deducting the share of Zakat) according to their respective shares. An old and one-eyed animal should not be taken in zakat"," nor should a bull be taken unless the giver of zakat so wishes. The rate of silver (in Zakat) is two hundred dirhams. Fortieth part of it is Zakat. If someone has one hundred and ninety dirhams"," Zakat is not obligatory on him unless the owner wants to pay it himself. And the one whose camels have a jiza (a four-year-old camel) wajib in zakat and he does not have a jiza but has a haqq (a young three-year-old camel)"," then the haqq and two goats will be collected from him"," provided that the goats are easily available"," or twenty dirhams will be collected. And one whose zakat includes Haqqa (a three-year-old young camel) but he does not have a three-year-old young camel but has a Jizah (a four-year-old camel)"," then the same Jizah (a four-year-old camel) will be collected from him"," but the recipient of the Zakat will give him twenty dirhams or two goats. (Narrated by Bukhari. )."""
"485","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him (by appointing an agent) to Yemen and ordered him to receive a one-year-old calf or heifer from every thirty cows and a Musnah (two-toothed cow or ox) from every forty. And take from every adult male a dinar or its equivalent of a piece of cloth (as tribute). (Narrated by all five. The words of the text are Ahmad's and Tirmidhi classifies it as Hasan and points out the disagreement about its reception, and it is said to be Sahih by both Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim.)"
"486","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuayb) and he from his grandfather (Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Zakat will be collected from the Muslims at their watering places.\"""""
"487","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no zakat (obligation) on a Muslim on his (servant) slave and on his (riding) horse.\"""""
"488","Hazrat Bahz bin Hakeem narrates from his father and he (Hakim) from his (Bahz) grandfather, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For every forty camels that graze in the forest, there is one Bint Lubun (two-year-old female camel) and they will not be separated on their account. A person who pays Zakat with the intention of getting reward, then for him there is reward and reward. And whoever withholds Zakat, We will forcefully collect from him and take half of his wealth (and more). This is one of the duties of our Lord. There is no share in it for the family of Muhammad.''"
"489","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you have two hundred dirhams and a whole year has passed on them"," five dirhams of Zakat is due on them.\"" And nothing is obligatory on you even if you have twenty dinars and a whole year has passed on them"," then half of them is zakat. If it is more than that"," then Zakat will be paid on it according to the same calculation. There is no zakat on any wealth until a whole year has passed on it.” (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and it is good. The imams differed on its abrogation.) And in Tirmidhi"," it is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (may God be pleased with him) that the person who received wealth (the wealth gained during the year) has no zakat before the year has passed. And the reason is that this tradition is suspended."""
"490","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that Zakat is not obligatory on working oxen. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and Daraqtani. It is Rajah that it is also muquf.)"
"491","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father and he from his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever becomes the guardian of a wealthy orphan"," he should invest the orphan's wealth in trade.\"" Don't let it lie idle like this so that the Zakat will eat it up.\"""""
"492","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Abi Ufa (may Allah be pleased with him) that when people came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Zakat, he used to pray for them like this. Ya Allah! Have mercy on them.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"493","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali (RA) that Hazrat Abbas (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether Zakat can be paid before its due time. So you gave them permission. (Narrated by Tirmidhi and Hakim)."
"494","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no Zakat on silver less than five ounces.\"" And there is no Zakat on less than five camels. And there is no zakat on dates less than five wasaqs. (The original of the tradition of Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri"," may Allah be pleased with him) is in Bukhari and Muslim."""
"495","Hazrat Salem bin Abdullah, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father. He narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \The land that is irrigated by the sky (rain) and springs"," or it is irrigated by itself (by drawing water from the roots)"," one-tenth (usr) is zakat"," and the land that is irrigated by drawing water is one-twentieth.\"" I have: \""If the land is moist (which does not need to be irrigated)"," it has an usher"," and if it is irrigated by drawing water from animals (or buckets)"," it is a twentieth part (half an usher).\"""""
"496","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Musa Ash'ari and Mu'adh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: \Do not collect zakat on any grain other than barley"," wheat"," raisins"," and dates.\"" (Narrated by Tabarani and Al-Hakim.) Zakat has been waived in sugarcane. (The authenticity of this tradition is weak.)"""
"497","Hazrat Sahl bin Abi Hatmah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: “When you make an estimate and guess (of the fruits on the trees), then (you can pick their fruit and then) receive the Zakat according to the estimate and leave a third part (of the estimated fruit). If you cannot leave the third part, then leave the fourth part."
"498","Hazrat Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us: “Grapes (unripe fruits) should also be assessed in the same way as dates are assessed. And their zakat should be received in the form of raisins.”"
"499","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr) that a woman came to the service of the Prophet. His daughter was also with him. And the daughter had two gold bracelets in her hand. He asked this woman: \Do you give her Zakat?\"" She said no. He said: \""Do you like that on the Day of Resurrection"," Allah should wear two bracelets of fire instead of them?\"" After hearing this"," the woman threw away both bracelets. (It has been narrated by all three. Its chain of transmission is strong"," and Hakim has narrated it on the authority of Hazrat Aisha"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and called it authentic.)"""
"500","It is narrated from Hazrat Umm Salamah that she used to wear gold anklets. He inquired, O Messenger of Allah! What: Is it Kunz? He said: \When you have paid his zakat"," then it is not kinaz.\"""""
"501","It was narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order us to collect Zakat from trading goods. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
"502","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is Khums (fifth share) in the buried treasure.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"503","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father and he from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a treasure that a man found in a desolate place: “If you find this treasure in an inhabited place, announce it for investigation. And if you found it in an uninhabited place, then it is a fifth part in it and in Raqaz.”"
"504","It was narrated from Hazrat Bilal bin Harith (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) received Zakat from the mines located in Qabul. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud.)"
"505","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered every slave, free, male, female, young and old, to give one saa of dates or one saa as Sadaqah al-Fitr to every Muslim. And it has been ordered that it should be paid before going out for Salah (Eid). (Bukhari and Muslim) In Ibn Udi and Darqutni, it is with a weak chain of transmission: “On this (Eid) day, make them (the poor) free from wandering around the village.”"
"506","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to give one Sa'a (Fitrana) of grains (wheat), dates, barley or raisins. (Bukhari and Muslim) And there is a hadith: \Or he used to take out a saa from the cheese.\"" Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said"," \""I will always take out the same amount that I used to take out during the time of the Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace.\"" And it is in the tradition of Abu Dawood: I will always take out only one sa'a."""
"507","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prescribed Sadaqah al-Fitr (Al-Fitr) to cleanse the fasting person from lewdness and obscenity and to feed the poor. Whoever pays it before offering the prayer, then it is acceptable, and whoever pays it after the prayer, then it is one of the (common) sadaqahs. (Not Sadaqah al-Fitr.) (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah, and Hakim said it to be Sahih.)"
"508","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah will place seven types of people in His shadow"," and on that day there will be no other shadow except His shadow.\"" Then he narrated the complete hadith. And in it is that (among these seven men is also that man:) \""Who gives charity so secretly that his left hand does not even know what his right hand has spent.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"509","It was narrated from Hazrat Uqba bin Aamir (RA) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “Every man will stand in the shadow of his charity until the people are judged.” (Narrated by Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim)."
"510","Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Whoever clothes a naked Muslim, Allah will clothe him with the green clothes of Paradise.” And whoever feeds a hungry Muslim, Allah will feed him with the fruits of Paradise. And the Muslim who gives (water or drink) to a thirsty Muslim, Allah will make him drink from the pure sealed wine of Paradise."
"511","Hazrat Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand. And start (almsgiving) with those whom he supports and takes care of. And the best charity is that which the giver remains rich after giving. Whoever refrains from asking questions, Allah will save him. And the one who shows indifference, Allah will make him indifference.\""512""","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was asked which charity is best. He said: \Giving charity to those who have little wealth through hard work.\"" And begin charity with those whose maintenance you are responsible for.”"""
"513","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Give charity and charity.\"" A man said: O Messenger of Allah! I have one dinar. He said: \""Spend it on your life.\"" He said: \""I have another.\"" He said: \""Spend it on your children.\"" He then said: I have another. He said: \""Spend it on your wife.\"" He then said"," \""I have another.\"" He said: \""Spend it on your servant.\"" He said: I have another. He said: \""He knows better about spending it.\"""""
"514","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “A woman who gives charity from the food of her house, provided that her intention is not to spoil the house, then she will surely get the reward and reward for what she gives in charity and her husband will also be rewarded because of what he earns.” And in the same way the treasurer will be rewarded, and the reward of one will not diminish the reward of another.\ (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"515","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) that Hazrat Zainab (RA) the wife of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masood (RA) came and said: O Messenger of Allah! You have ordered to give charity today. I have my personal jewelry, I want to give it as charity, but Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) thinks that he and his children are more deserving of giving charity to them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) has said the right thing.\"" Your husband and your children are more deserving of your charity.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"""
"516","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A man who always asks questions and begs people"," he will come on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that there will be no flesh on his face.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"517","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever asks people for their wealth (not out of necessity but) with the intention of increasing his wealth"," he is asking for the coals (of Hell) for himself.\"" Now it is his will whether he reduces them or increases them.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"""
"518","On the authority of Hazrat Zubayr bin Al-Awam, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you holds a rope, then carries a bundle of wood (from the forest) on his back and sells it, so that Allah may protect his honor and dignity, then this is better for him than asking whether people should give it to him or not.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"519","It is narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \To ask a question is like inflicting a wound and scratching"," with which a person injures his face"," except for the person who questions the head of state or asks because of compulsion.\"""""
"520","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Zakah (and Zakat) is not lawful for a rich and wealthy person except for five types of people. 1. Collector of Zakat and Sadaqah. 2. The (wealthy) person who buys charity with his wealth. 3. Indebtedness. 4. One who fights in the way of Allah. 5. Alms was given to a poor person and he gave it as a gift to a rich and wealthy man."""
"521","Hazrat Ubaidullah bin Udi bin Khiyar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that two men narrated to him their incident that they both attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (while he was distributing charity). They both asked him for charity. You took a look at them both from top to bottom and found them both powerful. He said: \If you wish"," I will give it to you"," but (the fact is) there is no share in it for the rich and powerful who can eat the earnings.\"""""
"522","On the authority of Hazrat Qubaysa bin Makhariq Hilali, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Questioning is permissible only for three people: A person who has taken a guarantee"," then it is permissible for him (the guarantor) to question it until he obtains that much money (by questioning) then he stops questioning.\"" And secondly"," a man who is beset by a sudden calamity which destroys his wealth"," it is permissible for him to ask until he has enough money to support himself. And thirdly"," the person who is surrounded by poverty and hunger"," and three wise men of his people testify that such and such a person is really in a state of poverty and hunger"," then it is permissible for him to question even if he has enough money with which he is able to earn his livelihood. And for people other than them"," O Qabaisa! Asking and asking is forbidden. Whatever the beggar obtains by asking"," he will eat forbidden wealth.” (Narrated by Muslim"," Abu Dawud"," Ibn Khuzimah and Ibn Hibban)."""
"523","On the authority of Hazrat Abdul Muttalib bin Rabi'ah bin Harith, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Undoubtedly"," charity is not suitable for the family of Muhammad (peace be upon him). It is a waste of people's (wealths)\"" and in another hadith: \""Charity is not lawful for Hazrat Muhammad (peace be upon him) and the family of Muhammad (peace be upon him).\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
"524","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Jubayr bin Mut'am (may Allah be pleased with him) that I and Hazrat Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! You gave the Banu Matla a share of the Khums of Khyber and neglected us, even though we and they are equal in relation to you. (On hearing this) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Banu Matal and Banu Hashim are one and the same thing.” (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"525","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Rafi' that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a man from Banu Makhzoom to collect alms and zakat. He said to Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him, \Come with me"," you will also get a share of it.\"" He said: I will not go until I come to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and inquire about it. So he came to his service and inquired from him"," and he said: \""The freed slave of the nation is also in him"," and charity and zakat are not lawful for us.\"""""
"526","Hazrat Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from his father (Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would give something to Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would say: Give it to those who are poorer than me. In response to this, he used to say: \Take it\"" then make it your wealth or give it as charity and take whatever wealth comes to you without greed or begging"," and do not set yourself after what is not found in this way.\"" (Narrated by Muslim)."""
